From 4c71ba4ed39a5c9c4888e7daf8491de367e2f9ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 02:47:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/52] ppc32: double<->int conversions without the 64-bit FPU
 (G3/G4 support)

12.4 re-derivation of the 9.4-series patch 0025 (same design and
mostly the same hunks; TurboAssembler merged into MacroAssembler):

- int32/uint32 -> double/float: ConvertIntToDoubleNoFPU64, the classic
  exponent-bias trick (build 2^52 + value' as raw words, subtract the
  bias; exact in all steps, frsp for the float variants), replacing
  MovIntToDouble+fcfid and superseding the interim fcfid+frsp form of
  the fcfids patch.
- TryInlineTruncateDoubleToI and the Generate_DoubleToI fast path:
  fctiwz via new ConvertDoubleToInt32 with an FPSCR[VXCVI] validity
  check (mtfsb0/mcrfs); invalid inputs fall through to the existing
  bit-twiddling slow path.
- kPPC_DoubleToInt32 needs NOTHING at 12.4: upstream's own
  DOUBLE_TO_INT32(fctiwz) macro plus the isel-fallback patch already
  produce exactly the 9.4 semantics (fctiwz, VXCVI -> zero result).
- kPPC_DoubleToUint32: upstream's DOUBLE_TO_INT32(fctiwuz) emits an
  ISA 2.06 instruction that sweep64 cannot see through the macro
  parameter (the known token-pasting blind spot); replaced on 32-bit
  with the proven two-range sequence ([0,2^31) direct; [2^31,2^32)
  converts input-2^31 and restores the top bit).
- kPPC_DoubleToInt64: the case is now PPC64-only.  Unlike 9.4 (which
  kept a dead fctidz case) an emission on 32-bit fails loudly in the
  code generator, consistent with the generic-selector UNSUPPORTED
  philosophy; 64-bit machine ops do not exist in 32-bit graphs
  (Int64Lowering / C-call wrappers replace them).
---
